Package: kulan-settings
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @PUBLISHER@ <@MAINTAINER_EMAIL@>
Section: gnome
Priority: optional
Depends: kulan-base (= @VERSION@), kulan-update-center (= @VERSION@), python3 (>= 3.11), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.12), gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), gir1.2-nm-1.0, gir1.2-secret-1, qrencode, gir1.2-gstreamer-1.0, gir1.2-gst-plugins-base-1.0, gir1.2-gst-plugins-bad-1.0, gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-nice, gstreamer1.0-pipewire, xdg-desktop-portal
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal-gnome, gnome-control-center, gir1.2-goa-1.0, gnome-shell, gnome-user-share, rygel, libegl1, libgles2, upower, bluez, power-profiles-daemon, accountsservice, locales, openssl, gnome-remote-desktop, cups, cups-client, kulan-desktop-settings (= @VERSION@), fprintd, libpam-fprintd
Breaks: kulan-update-center (<< 2.2~)
Replaces: kulan-update-center (<< 2.2~)
Homepage: @HOME_URL@
Description: @NAME@ Settings
 One place for @NAME@ options: appearance, wallpaper, the dock, the top
 bar, displays, keyboard, login items, add-ons and About @NAME@.
 .
 It includes Software Update, which replaces Update Center: available
 updates, what's new, update history, automatic updates and restore points.
 Wi-Fi and network, Bluetooth, Sound, Battery and power, Displays, and
 Sharing (remote desktop, files and media) and Online accounts (Google and
 Microsoft 365) are built in too.
 .
 On computers in an organisation (Kulan Fleet), Get help sends what's
 wrong (and a screenshot, if the person adds one) to the organisation's
 admins, and it offers remote help: an admin can see the screen, and control
 it if allowed, only after the person at the computer agrees.
